  "body": "## What changed\nAdds one test to `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs` (plus a small fixture helper) pinning that changing only `taper_deg` changes the wire contour stamp, for a punch path and an open run, and that the machine's maximum taper (`edm.max_taper_deg`) moves a tapered stamp. No product code changed.\n\n## Readings\nThe stamp digests a stated taper in `crates/app/src/operation/params.rs` (the taper tag and value) and, for a tapered cut, the machine maximum in `crates/app/src/operation/wire_op.rs`. The test shows both inputs are live.\n\n## Pinning test\n- `a_taper_alone_moves_the_stamp_and_so_does_the_machine_maximum` (exact, `camcraft-app` / `wire_stamp`): passes on the branch.\n\n## Mutation check\nDropped the taper digest in `params.rs` (`if false && p.taper_deg != 0.0`). The test fails at the 2-vs-3 degree assertion (`Punch: 2 and 3 degrees must stamp apart`), so the test catches it. The source was restored (`git checkout`), the tree is clean.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_stamp -- a_taper_alone_moves_the_stamp_and_so_does_the_machine_maximum --exact`: ok (1 passed).\n- Mutation check as above: fails as expected.\n- Branch merged with `origin/main` (merge commit `9cb4cdff3`) before the test run.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The quick gate tier and clippy were not run (only the pinning test, per the brief).\n- The rest of `wire_stamp` and the other suites were not run.\n- Mutation of `wire_op.rs` alone was not tried.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1380\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
